Z||000000||beachbomb||06-17-2001||12:34 PM||||Well, i went to the bone-yard today, first time in about 4 months, i saw a total of 5 fieros there, 1 '88 coupe, 3 '87's all coupes and 1 '86 SE, the 88 still had its suspension and looked to be in good shape, engine was removed, those '88 suspensions are ALOT different than my '84's(first time i've seen one up close!, so after moving on from that one, the next one i saw was an original paint job BLUE '87 Coupe, most body panels looked to be in good condition, only bad spots i saw on the paint was fading on the roof, cradle was dropped, engine was on ground and trans was gone, again first time i've seen an original blue paint job(i told the owner of the junk yard i would have bought the entire car when it first came in the yard if i had only known!!) he told me i could take body panels off if i wanted, i tole him i might, anyway, the other cars where normal coupes except the '86 had the v-6 in it(small engine fire on this one)..if you really need any parts off these e-mail me and i'll see what i can do. These cars are located in JAx florida, Jim(2 '84 Indys)<BR>p.s. please keep in mind i only have normal tools, so suspension removal is probably out of the question.||||reg||9
